#
# AROSTCP network service: MIDI over the network (netmidid).
#
# AppleMIDI (RTP-MIDI) sessions on UDP 5004 and 5005, and Network MIDI 2.0
# sessions on the port its configuration gives, if it gives one. It
# answers invitations, invites the peers it is configured to, and
# advertises itself through the mDNS service. CAMD clients reach its peers
# through the ports of the drivers DEVS:Midi/applemidi and
# DEVS:Midi/networkmidi2. It takes no arguments: what it does is in its
# configuration, ENV:NetMIDI.
#
#   Path    - the daemon executable
#   Order   - bring-up priority hint (higher starts earlier): after mDNS
#   StopSig - signal bit sent to stop it (12 = CTRL-C)
#   Policy  - restart: across a reconfiguration of the stack it is stopped
#             and started again, and its sessions with it
#   Enabled - yes or no
#
Name=Network MIDI
Path=SYS:System/Network/Services/netmidid
Order=10
StopSig=12
Policy=restart
Enabled=yes
